BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OCAD U x Tonkin Liu Design Talk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T200000
UID:ocad-u-x-tonkin-liu-design-talk@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join Tonkin Liu\, the award-winning studio working across arch
 itecture\, art\, and landscape\, for a special talk exploring the creative
  possibilities of learning from nature.\n\nOCAD U x Tonkin Liu - Design Ta
 lk Date/Time: Tuesday\, October 27\, 2026\, 6:00 - 8:00 p.m. Location: RBC
  Centre for Emerging Artists & Designers (CEAD)\, 115 McCaul St.\, Level 3
  RSVP to attend Join Tonkin Liu \, the award-winning studio working across
  architecture\, art\, and landscape\, for a special talk exploring the cre
 ative possibilities of learning from nature. Their global practice brings 
 storytelling and technical invention together to create places that engage
  the senses and respond to their surroundings. Their new book\, Asking\, L
 ooking\, Playing\, Making: A Nature-Focused Design Process \, opens up thi
 s approach\, revealing how curiosity and experimentation turn initial idea
 s into buildings rooted in place.
LOCATION:Rosalie Sharp Pavillion (MCD) 115 McCaul St. Level 3
URL:https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/H8eiaeBjAQ
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing Disco
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T210059
UID:drawing-disco@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:A party-meets-performance drawing event\, "Drawing Disco" brin
 gs art\, music\, and movement together for a playful night of drawing. Par
 t of the three-day art festival Drawing Out: Art Now.\n\nDrawing Disco\n\n
 Drawing Out: Art Now - Drawing Disco Come join Drawing Disco \, a special 
 fundraiser supporting OCAD University Faculty of Art students. Your partic
 ipation helps future artists move forward in their careers and creates opp
 ortunities for co-curricular activities and professional development. Draw
 ing Disco is part of Drawing Out: Art Now \, an art festival curated by Ja
 mes Olley and Amy Swartz celebrating OCAD University's 150-year legacy. In
 vited artist Erin Finley is leading an immersive\, playful night on Octobe
 r 27 \, featuring participatory live drawing with a disco-inspired spirit.
  It’s a creative experience you won’t want to miss as we celebrate one
  of Canada’s largest art institutions. Art lovers of all levels are welc
 ome. No drawing experience required! Drawing supplies have been generously
  sponsored by Above Ground Art Supplies and are all ready for you. Just le
 t your inner child free and draw\, play\, dance\, and have fun. Come glam 
 it up! Tuesday\, October 27: Drawing Disco 6:00 - 9:00 PM OCAD University\
 , The Great Hall\n\nA party-meets-performance drawing event. Erin Finley's
  drawing practice demystifies traditional drawing\, viewing mark-making as
  an accessible\, therapeutic human action. Ultimately\, her work transform
 s drawing into a community-centered performance\, fostering neuroplasticit
 y\, shared resilience\, and collective joy. Ticket Here (Includes 1Free Dr
 ink\, Hors d'Oeuvres\, Drawing Supplies\, Door Prizes) Space limited!!! 19
 + event Drawing supplies included + 2 raffle door prizes worth $250 each! 
 Additional donations can be made during the event to support OCAD U art st
 udents further.\n\nSpecial thanks to Aiyana Alzamora and Celine Fu for the
  design.
LOCATION:The Great Hall 100 McCaul St.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/drawing-disco
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drawing Out: Art Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T235959
UID:drawing-out-art-now@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:A three-day Art festival curated by James Olley and Amy Swartz
  marking OCAD University's 150-year legacy through performance\, participa
 tion\, and expanded approaches to drawing.\n\nDrawing Out: Art Now\n\nDraw
 ing Out: Art Now is a three-day Art festival curated by James Olley and Am
 y Swartz marking OCAD University's 150-year legacy through performance\, p
 articipation\, and expanded approaches to drawing. The program foregrounds
  contemporary art practices in which gesture\, movement\, and live action 
 intersect with mark-making. In this context\, drawing is an act of movemen
 t: a way of thinking\, understanding\, and making through the body\, becom
 ing both process and trace. Tuesday\, October 27: Drawing Disco 6:00 - 9:0
 0 PM Wednesday\, October 28: Drawing in 4 Parts 1:30 - 4:30 PM Thursday\, 
 October 29: Drawing to a Close 5:30 - 8:30 PM OCAD University\, The Great 
 Hall\n\nDrawing Disco\n\nA party-meets-performance drawing event. Erin Fin
 ley's drawing practice demystifies traditional drawing\, viewing mark-maki
 ng as an accessible\, therapeutic human action. Ultimately\, her work tran
 sforms drawing into a community-centered performance\, fostering neuroplas
 ticity\, shared resilience\, and collective joy. Tuesday\, October 27\, 6 
 to 9 PM Ticket Here (Includes 1Free Drink\, Hors d'Oeuvres\, Drawing Suppl
 ies\, Door Prizes) Space limited!!! 19+ event\n\nDrawing in 4 Parts A seri
 es of performances and installations exploring drawing through paper\, scu
 lpture\, material transformation\, and durational processes. Wednesday\, O
 ctober 28\, 1:30 to 4:30 PM Free Admissions\n\nDrawing to a Close\n\nPerfo
 rmance-based works exploring identity\, memory\, gesture\, storytelling\, 
 and social exchange through expanded drawing practices. Thursday\, October
  29\, 5 to 8 PM Pay what you can\n\nHonouring Cathy Daley: Performance by 
 James Knott\n\nSpecial thanks to Aiyana Alzamora and Celine Fu for the des
 ign.
LOCATION:The Great Hall 100 McCaul St.
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/drawing-out-art-now
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Week!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261027T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261029T235959
UID:wellness-week@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Free food\, raffles/prizes\, workshops and more!\n\nA 3-day Ev
 ent: October 27-29\n\nFollow us on Instagram to keep up with updates!\n\nT
 he Student Wellness Centre will be hosting a 3-day wellness event this yea
 r. There will be food\, activities\, prizes and an opportunity to learn ab
 out the different resources available to OCAD U students.\n\nCheck out wha
 t we will be offering each day below. We hope to see you there!\n\nWellnes
 s Tabling Event October 27th 11 a.m. to 4 p.m. 100 McCaul St.\, Main Lobby
  We will be hosting a tabling event providing students with academic\, men
 tal/physical health resources! There will be free hot lunch\, activities a
 nd a chance to enter our raffle for giveaways such as gift cards and Saje 
 wellness bundles. Who you can expect! Student Wellbeing Centre for Learnin
 g & Teaching International Student's Office Alumo Good2Talk Campus Life We
 st Toronto Ontario Health Team\n\nHarm Reduction Workshop October 28th 12 
 p.m. 230 Richmond St W.\, Student Living Room (8F) The SWC within OCAD U h
 as partnered with local community health centres\, other colleges and univ
 ersities to begin connecting with students about Harm Reduction. Come join
  us for a free pizza lunch and meet some of our partners who are doing ama
 zing Harm Reduction work in Toronto. The workshop will allow for students 
 to learn and ask questions about Harm Reduction (ie: safer drug use practi
 ces\, the toxic toronto drug supply\, nalaxone\, drug prohibition/mass inc
 arceration\, HIV and Hep C) and to provide input on how the wellness centr
 e can implement this program effectively. Workshop led by Chance Cordon\, 
 Manager\, Harm Reduction Project.\n\nDecompression Day October 29th 10 a.m
 . to 6 p.m. 230 Richmond St W.\, Student Living Room (8F) As important as 
 it is to be proactive with your wellness\, sometimes its about decompressi
 ng and winding down. Come by the Student Living Room to enjoy a relaxing a
 ctivity day. There will be paint-your-own mugs (while supplies last)\, sna
 cks and vibey music.
LOCATION:Main Building & Rosalie Sharp Centre for Design (MCA) 100 McCaul 
 Street & Student Living Room
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/wellness-week
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
